<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Apple's privacy manifest. Required for App Store submission since 1 May 2024;
  a build without one is rejected at upload.

  `ios/` is generated by `npx cap add ios` on every CI run and is gitignored,
  so this file lives here and `scripts/patch-ios-project.mjs` copies it in.

  WHAT IS DECLARED, AND WHY EACH ANSWER IS WHAT IT IS — Apple's definition of
  "collect" is "transmit off the device", which is narrower than it sounds and
  is what makes most of this list empty:

  · Location is READ and never collected. NearbyDial, CoordinatePicker and
    /add ask for a fix, sort the 52 places by distance on the device, and throw
    it away. Nothing posts it anywhere — there is no back end to post it to
    (supabaseEnabled is false). So it belongs in the usage strings, not here.

  · Audio IS collected, and is the only thing that is. A شوق call streams the
    microphone to ElevenLabs to be transcribed. It is not linked to an identity
    — the app has no accounts — and it is not used for tracking.

  · No tracking, and no tracking domains. There is no analytics SDK, no
    advertising identifier and no third-party measurement anywhere in the
    bundle. NSPrivacyTracking false is a claim `audit:ios` re-checks against
    the built export rather than a promise made once.

  · UserDefaults is reached by Capacitor's own runtime, not by wain. CA92.1 is
    the reason code for "access solely to store or read data for the app
    itself", which is exactly what a WebView shell does with it.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
  <false/>

  <key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
  <array/>

  <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
  <array>
    <dict>
      <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
      <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeAudioData</string>
      <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
      <false/>
      <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
      <false/>
      <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
      <array>
        <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
      </array>
    </dict>
  </array>

  <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
  <array>
    <dict>
      <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
      <string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
      <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
      <array>
        <string>CA92.1</string>
      </array>
    </dict>
  </array>
</dict>
</plist>
